solving a hard puzzle in a game can make  you feel like a genius but getting stuck  on one can frustrate you to the point of  throwing the controller and quitting the  game for good in the last decade we've  seen a number of puzzles and games that  have challenged our brains and even  brought the gaming community together to  figure them out here are four of the  most challenging puzzles in gaming  brought to you by America's Navy  the intricate puzzles in Fez required  serious dedication to solve but none  more so than the black monolith puzzle  if you're a completionist your mission  is to collect all the special cubes in  the game including three secret red  cubes to get the final red cube you need  to figure out the secret of the black  monolith you won't be able to find the  puzzle in your first playthrough beat  the game to unlock the ability to look  around in first person then once you're  in the right room you have to use your  new ability to stand on a blank Square  and input a specific code to activate  the monolith the problem it's impossible  to figure out on your own players in the  Fez community had to band together to  figure out the code and test every  single possibility once you put in the  code the mysterious floating block  appears and now you have to figure out  what to do with it  fezzes development team leaked clues  that another code had to be entered  somewhere else in the room it took the  Fez community over 66,000 tries to  figure it out so you have their tireless  work to think if you've got the time you  could try to crack the code yourself but  if not mindless walkthroughs was kind  enough to create a walkthrough video  with a code on screen red cubes for  everyone about halfway through  Dishonored 2 during the 6th mission you  find yourself in the dust district here  you will come across the jinn - Locke  which keeps you from getting into  stilton's Manor the jinn - Locke is a  combination lock that requires you to  match a set of names with a set of  symbols figuring out the combination of  the lock allows you to skip most of the  dust district mission so how do you do  it to the right on the door you will  find the jinn - riddle which spells out  the solution to the lock combination if  you're stumped by the riddle and you try  to look up the solution online you're  out of luck the riddle and its details  are randomized for each game so someone  else's solution will not work for you  tough break time to crack some codes  while it is possible to test out every  possible combination that would take a  really long time the jinn - riddle is a  logic grid puzzle that contains short  word problems game crate built one that  you can find on their site the trick is  to figure out the relationship between  the different elements mentioned within  the riddle and while figuring out the  solution may not really save you any  time overall you do get an achievement  for solving it called Eureka  portal brought us unique gameplay that  challenged our perspective and  problem-solving abilities figuring out  how to use the portals to traverse  through each level forces you to think  differently and really tests your  spatial awareness the hardest portal  test chamber by far is chamber 18 where  all the skills you have developed up  until that point are put to the test  YouTube user x12 ozx demonstrates how to  move through the chamber in this video  making it look easy and making me feel  really dumb carefully place your portals  to move up the levels in the chamber you  come across a door to the exit in order  to open it you need a cube to hold down  the button getting the cube involves  figuring out this mess of a room get  through the androids get across the room  get the cube and get back to the button  to hold it down but wait there's more as  if getting the cube wasn't hard enough  you have to quickly ascend platforms and  shoot portals in midair in order to get  to the top and finish the level  [Music]  last on our list is a puzzle game so  challenging that I quit halfway through  and never went back the witness is a 3d  puzzle game that involves exploring an  open world you progress by navigating  mazes and solving puzzles that each have  their own set of rules with clues  scattered around the island or within  the environment some puzzles have no  clues at all there are around 650  puzzles in the witness but fortunately  you don't have to solve all of them to  finish the game while the entire game  belongs on this list one section of  puzzles in particular is the most  difficult and mentally exhausting the  infamous challenge the challenge is an  optional set of puzzles located inside  the mountain it's a time-based challenge  that requires completing 14 randomized  puzzles within 7 minutes to solve the  puzzles you must draw on the rules you  have learned throughout the game it's  impossible to cheat off a walkthrough as  someone else's puzzles won't be the same  set you end up with as ps4 trophies  demonstrates here head deep into the  mountain to find the challenge solve  this pillar then make your way through  the area until you find the music box to  start the challenge music will start to  play if you have not solved all the  puzzles by the time the music stops you  will fail  if you screw up I need to start over the  puzzles are randomly generated and will  be different every time it's incredibly  stressful those are four of the most  challenging puzzles in gaming brought to  you by America's new  what do you think the hardest pozzolan  gaming is let me know in the comments  below and thanks for watching  [Music]
 

